# Work from the code

Edit the code and stop. Do not open the browser, lock the page, reload it, scroll it, or screenshot it to confirm a change you can already judge from the code.

- Open the page only when the fix cannot be judged from the code. Look only at the one section the user pointed at, then stop.
- Change only the reported problem. Do not check other widths, other pages, or nearby sections.
- Fold a small mismatch into the same edit. Do not open a second pass.
- This overrides the habit of verifying every UI change in the browser.
